@@ -134,8 +134,8 @@
             <h2>Features that are gone, or were never there</h2>
             <div class="platform-grid">
                 <div class="platform-card" id="claim-5">
-                    <h3>No drums, sampler instrument, video editing, livestream or audio recorder</h3>
-                    <p>All of these were either removed deliberately or never wired up. There is no drum machine, no sampler instrument, no video capture or editing, no livestreaming (RTMP was scoped and cut &mdash; never built), and, up to version 10.79.492, no audio recorder &mdash; that build has no microphone input. What the Workstation does have is new and still being tested on devices: it arranges parts on tracks, imports .mid and audio files, edits MIDI notes and records MIDI takes from a controller. From the next version on it can also record the microphone onto one audio track you armed yourself; that is still being tested on devices and is not claimed until it is confirmed there.</p>
+                    <h3>No drums, sampler instrument, video editing or audio recorder; livestream not yet confirmed</h3>
+                    <p>All of these were either removed deliberately or never wired up. There is no drum machine, no sampler instrument, no video capture or editing, no livestreaming you can rely on yet (RTMP streaming is built and being tested &mdash; not yet confirmed on a device), and, up to version 10.79.492, no audio recorder &mdash; that build has no microphone input. What the Workstation does have is new and still being tested on devices: it arranges parts on tracks, imports .mid and audio files, edits MIDI notes and records MIDI takes from a controller. From the next version on it can also record the microphone onto one audio track you armed yourself; that is still being tested on devices and is not claimed until it is confirmed there.</p>
                 </div>
                 <div class="platform-card" id="claim-11">
                     <h3>No voice processing: no cloning, AI voice, text-to-speech or autotune</h3>
@@ -170,8 +170,8 @@
             <h2>What it is built on</h2>
             <div class="platform-grid">
                 <div class="platform-card" id="claim-8">
-                    <h3>Zero external dependencies &mdash; so also zero of the usual suspects</h3>
-                    <p>Echoelmusic ships with no third-party packages at all. That means no Composable Architecture, no RevenueCat, no SwiftData, no VideoToolbox and no HaishinKit &mdash; several of which have been attributed to it. It is Swift, SwiftUI, and Apple frameworks, plus open standards on the wire: OSC, ADM-OSC, Art-Net, sACN and MIDI.</p>
+                    <h3>Two third-party packages, for streaming only &mdash; and none of the usual suspects</h3>
+                    <p>Until October&nbsp;2026 Echoelmusic shipped with no third-party packages at all. It now links exactly two, both BSD-3 and both used only when you start a stream: HaishinKit&nbsp;2.2.5 (RTMP / RTMPS) and its logger Logboard&nbsp;2.6.0. Streaming itself is built and being tested &mdash; not yet confirmed on a device. There is still no Composable Architecture, no RevenueCat, no SwiftData, no VideoToolbox, no SRT or WebRTC stack, and no analytics, advertising or tracking SDK. Everything else is Swift, SwiftUI and Apple frameworks, plus open standards on the wire: OSC, ADM-OSC, Art-Net, sACN and MIDI.</p>
                 </div>
             </div>
         </section>
