-    <script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What is Echoelmusic?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Echoelmusic is a bio-reactive generative music instrument that transforms your biometric signals (heart rate, HRV, breathing) into harmonic, melodic and rhythmic loops in real time, which you export as .wav or as a MIDI file (.mid) for your DAW. GPU bio-reactive visuals, Art-Net/sACN lighting output and a Workstation that arranges parts on tracks (note editor, .mid and audio import) ship today; video editing, audio recording and live broadcast are not part of it today. Coming to iPhone first, with iPad, Mac, Apple Watch, Apple TV and Vision Pro planned."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Which features are available at launch?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"At launch Echoelmusic is a bio-reactive music instrument: bio-reactive synthesis, generative composition of harmonic, melodic and rhythmic loops in any key and BPM, GPU/Metal bio-reactive visuals (flash-safe, in a movable floating window on the phone, full-screen on a connected display), Art-Net and sACN lighting output, export to .wav or .mid for Ableton, Logic and FL Studio, a Workstation that arranges parts on tracks with a note editor and .mid and audio import, MIDI input from an external controller plus MIDI note output to your rig, biometrics (HRV, heart rate, breath via HealthKit, Bluetooth straps like Polar H10, and camera rPPG), OSC and ADM-OSC sync, and coherence / self-observation. DMX-512 interfaces, projection mapping, on-device AI, spatial audio and Ableton Link are on the roadmap, not in the app today; video editing, audio recording and live streaming are not in the app today. See the Architecture page for exact current status."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What makes it bio-reactive?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"EchoelBio captures your biometrics — HRV, heart rate, breath, and coherence — and feeds them to the sound engine in real time. Your heart rate influences tempo, brightness and vibrato; coherence is the strongest single driver — brightness, filter cutoff, harmonic content, level and noise; HRV shifts brightness and overtone spread; breathing shapes the amplitude envelope."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What are the EchoelTools?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Shipping today: EchoelSynth (bio-reactive synthesis), EchoelGen (generative composition), EchoelFX (effects), EchoelMIDI (MIDI 2.0-ready input), EchoelBio (biometrics), EchoelNet (OSC/ADM-OSC), EchoelVis (GPU bio-reactive visuals), EchoelLux (Art-Net + sACN lighting). Live as well: EchoelStage external-display output (USB-C/HDMI or AirPlay). On the roadmap: projection mapping and EchoelAI (on-device intelligence). Cut: EchoelMix (console/multitrack) and EchoelVid (video editing and video recording) — both were built and removed."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do I need special hardware?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"For basic use, just your iPhone. Bio-reactive features work with the iPhone camera pulse (rPPG), an Apple Watch via Apple Health, or a Bluetooth heart-rate strap such as Polar H10 (any standard BLE heart-rate device works). Lighting rigs connect over Art-Net/sACN on your network; DMX-512 interfaces and smart-home lighting are on the roadmap."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Which platforms are supported?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"iOS 18 on iPhone at launch. iPad, Mac, Apple Watch, Apple TV and Vision Pro are planned; Android, Web PWA, Windows and Linux may follow later."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What synthesis engines are included?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"All synthesis is unified inside EchoelSynth — one tool with three voices: a DDSP harmonic-plus-noise core, a polyphonic pad/lead, and a dedicated sub-bass. Your biometrics compose harmonic and melodic material — pads, chords, leads and bass, with no drum layer and no sampler — rendered to .wav or exported as a MIDI file (.mid)."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How many effects are there?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"All effects are unified inside EchoelFX — one tool with a full range of effect types: filter, saturation, tape, bitcrush, chorus, flanger, phaser, tremolo, delay, reverb, stereo widener, compressor and limiter — all bio-modulatable. Zero external dependencies. Modelled analog compressors (VCA, Opto, FET, VariMu) are on the roadmap, not in the app."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What visual modes are available?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"GPU/Metal bio-reactive visuals ship today: four generative looks (Rings, Water, Aurora, Depth) driven live by heart rate, coherence and breath, and the picture is playable — touching it turns your fingers into notes quantized to the take's key and scale — in a movable floating window on the phone, or full-screen on a connected display (EchoelStage) for projection, flash-capped under 3 Hz and honouring Reduce Motion. Richer generative and AR worlds are the wider vision. Video recording, and video editing (NLE, ProRes, color grading), are not part of Echoelmusic — the editor was built and removed in July 2026, recording in September 2026."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I control lights and lasers?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes — Art-Net and sACN (E1.31) lighting output ship today: your heartbeat can drive a stage or venue rig natively over open standards, no vendor SDK, with flash safety built in. Echoelmusic also speaks OSC and ADM-OSC live for TouchDesigner or Resolume. External displays ship today (EchoelStage: USB-C/HDMI or AirPlay). DMX-512 interfaces, smart-home lighting and projection mapping are on the roadmap."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What AI features does Echoelmusic have?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"On-device AI is on the roadmap, not in the app today. The vision for EchoelAI is entirely on-device via CoreML — AI stem separation to isolate vocals, bass and instruments, with no cloud and full privacy. In active development."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I collaborate with others?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes — EchoelNet provides one-way OSC (Open Sound Control) output to DAWs, VJ software and custom applications, plus a virtual MIDI source (MIDI 1.0) that appears once you enable a MIDI route in the routing panel, with MPE output over it behind two routing switches. OSC control input ships too: a whitelist of /echoelmusic/ctrl/ cues (tempo while locked, key, scale, genre, visual look, blackout) plus ADM-OSC track positions (/adm/obj/n/) from a spatial controller, off by default. A full bidirectional OSC session and Ableton Link tempo sync are on the roadmap."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Who owns what I create?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"You do. 100%. Everything you create with Echoelmusic belongs entirely to you. No royalty claims, no usage restrictions."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How much does Echoelmusic cost?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Version 1.0 is free in full — the whole instrument, no ads, no tracking, no account. Later versions may add optional paid tiers aimed at live and professional use."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is this a medical device?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. Echoelmusic is a creative tool, not a medical device. Biofeedback features are for creative and self-observation purposes only."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is my data safe?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"All biometric data is processed locally on your device. No accounts, no analytics, no tracking or advertising SDKs. Your device's own on-device Data Protection encrypts local storage."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is Echoelmusic accessible?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"We build with accessibility in mind. Today the app provides VoiceOver labels on the primary controls, reduced-motion support, a dark high-contrast interface, and a 3 Hz visual-flash safety cap (WCAG epilepsy guidance). WCAG 2.2 AA is our target as the app grows; broader accessibility modes, color-vision options and more languages are planned, not in the app today. The app currently ships in English."}}]}</script>
